---
title: "process_transaction (Sui Whitepaper: Authority Base Operation)"
---
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    [*] --> q_check_epoch: receive Tx from client
    q_check_epoch --> q_check_inputs: epoch(Tx) == current_epoch
    q_check_epoch --> q_error_epoch: epoch(Tx) != current_epoch
    q_error_epoch --> [*]: return error

    q_check_inputs --> q_load_objects: all ObjRef in inputs(Tx) and payment(Tx) exist in Obj_v
    q_check_inputs --> q_error_inputs: missing object references
    q_error_inputs --> [*]: return error

    q_load_objects --> q_check_gas: load [Obj] from Obj_v
    q_check_gas --> q_check_valid: sufficient gas in payment object
    q_check_gas --> q_error_gas: insufficient gas
    q_error_gas --> [*]: return error

    q_check_valid --> q_check_locks: valid(Tx, [Obj]) == true
    q_check_valid --> q_error_auth: valid(Tx, [Obj]) == false
    q_error_auth --> [*]: return error

    q_check_locks --> q_set_locks: Lock_v[ObjRef] is None or same Tx for all owned inputs
    q_check_locks --> q_error_locked: Lock_v[ObjRef] set to different Tx
    q_error_locked --> [*]: return error

    q_set_locks --> q_sign: atomically set Lock_v[ObjRef] = TxSign for all owned inputs
    q_sign --> [*]: return TxSign (partial certificate)

    note right of q_check_locks
        INV-001: Lock_v[ObjRef] set to first valid Tx seen, no unlock within epoch
        INV-002: Authority signs at most one transaction per owned object version
        INV-003: Processing is idempotent upon success
    end note
